WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Registering on the electoral register takes a few minutes on GOV.UK. You will be asked for your National Insurance number (if you have one).

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:27.000
In England, British, Irish and Commonwealth citizens with leave to remain can register, as can citizens of Spain, Portugal, Poland, Denmark and Luxembourg; other EU citizens if they were already legally resident before 2021. In Scotland and Wales, any resident with leave.

3
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Being on the register helps your credit history (for renting or getting a phone on a contract). Rubbish: each council has its own collection days and bins (general, recycling, food, garden). Look it up on your council's website with your postcode.

4
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.600
Noisy neighbours: first talk to them politely; if it continues, the council can step in.

5
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.900
Say it aloud: “Which bin is for recycling?”.
